Fly a design (.ork, .hpr, .hprz or a rocket's .json) off a rail and print its flight; save its recording with --export

Usage: hpr sim [OPTIONS] <DESIGN>

Arguments:
  <DESIGN>
          The design: an OpenRocket .ork file, an HPR design (.hpr, or .hprz with its attachments), or a rocket's JSON (.json)

Options:
      --config <NAME>
          The motor configuration to fly: its number in the list the output shows, its name, or its id. Without it, the design's default flies, or its only one

      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text; errors too

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. Auto colors what goes to a terminal and heeds NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --motor <NAME_OR_FILE>
          Fly this motor in place of the configuration's, lit at launch: a catalog designation or common name, or a .eng or .rse file

      --mount <NAME>
          The motor mount that --motor goes in, by its name or its component id. Without it, the motor goes in the configuration's mount, or the design's only one

      --delay <S_OR_P>
          The ejection delay of --motor's motor: seconds from burnout to its charge (0 fires it at burnout), or P for a plugged motor. Without it, the motor fires no charge

      --latitude <DEG>
          The launch site's latitude, degrees north (south is negative)
          
          [default: 0]

      --longitude <DEG>
          The launch site's longitude, degrees east (west is negative)
          
          [default: 0]

      --elevation <M>
          The launch site's height above sea level, m
          
          [default: 0]

      --rail-length <M>
          The rail's length, m, from the rocket's aft end to the rail's top
          
          [default: 1.5]

      --inclination <DEG>
          The rail's angle above the horizon, degrees [default: 90, vertical]

      --heading <DEG>
          The direction the rail leans toward, degrees clockwise from true north [default: 0]

      --wind <M_S>
          A wind of this speed at every height, m/s [default: calm]

      --wind-from <DEG>
          The direction the wind blows from, degrees clockwise from true north
          
          [default: 0]

      --accept-design-errors
          Fly a design whose checks find errors, such as a motor wider than its mount

      --offline
          Take a motor the bundled catalog lacks from the cache of ThrustCurve.org only, never the network

      --export <FILE>
          Write the flight's recording to this file: .csv, .json, .parquet, .geojson or .kml (repeat for several)

      --plot <FILE>
          Draw the flight's altitude, speed and acceleration against time, its events marked, into this .svg file

      --interval <S>
          The recording's interval, s, at least 0.001; a row is also recorded at every event
          
          [default: 0.01]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Fly a design on the motor it was saved with:
      hpr sim my-rocket.ork
  Fly it on another motor, in a 4 m/s wind from the west:
      hpr sim my-rocket.ork --motor H170M --delay 10 --wind 4 --wind-from 270
  Save its recording and draw its altitude, speed and acceleration:
      hpr sim my-rocket.ork --export flight.csv --plot flight.svg

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-sim
